.TH XDP-BFD 8 "2026-09-15" "xdp-bfd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
xdp-bfd \- XDP-based BFD data plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xdp-bfd
.I local-ip peer-ip
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B xdp-bfd --dplane
.IR port | sock-path
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B xdp-bfd --check
.br
.B xdp-bfd --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdp-bfd
runs Bidirectional Forwarding Detection in the kernel with an XDP program.
It offloads the periodic transmit and the fast detection timers from FRR's
bfdd, so sub-second sessions scale without a userspace packet for every
tick.
.PP
In the usual deployment it attaches to FRR over the bfdd data-plane socket
with
.BR --dplane .
Given a local and a peer address instead, it runs a single static session
on its own. The XDP object is ABI-checked against the engine when it loads,
and the binary carries the object's install path, so it finds
.I /usr/lib/xdp-bfd/bfd_xdp.o
with no argument.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --dplane " port|sock-path"
Attach to FRR bfdd on the given data-plane port or Unix socket path.
.TP
.BI --dp-peer " user|uid"
The account bfdd runs as. With a Unix socket it owns the socket and, with
root, is the only account allowed to connect. Ignored for a TCP port.
.TP
.BI --dp-hold " sec"
Hold sessions this many seconds after bfdd disconnects (0-86400).
.TP
.BI --kernel-tx " if"
Transmit from the kernel on this interface.
.TP
.BI --bpf-obj " path"
Load the XDP object from this path instead of the compiled-in one.
.TP
.BI --xdp-mode " drv|generic"
Attach in native driver mode or generic (SKB) mode.
.TP
.BI --stats-dump " path"
Path a SIGUSR1 writes the stats snapshot to.
.TP
.BI --sweep-us " 500-100000"
Session sweep interval in microseconds.
.TP
.BI --tick-us " 200-100000"
Poll-loop tick in microseconds.
.TP
.BI --deadman-us " 0|50000-60000000"
Dead-man interval; 0 turns it off.
.TP
.BR --demand ", " --demand-poll-us " " \fI0|10000-600000000\fR
Demand mode and its poll interval; 0 turns the poll off.
.TP
.BI --auth " type:keyid:key"
Authenticate the static session. \fItype\fR is \fBsimple\fR,
\fBkeyed-sha1\fR or \fBmeticulous-sha1\fR; \fIkeyid\fR is 0-255 and
\fIkey\fR is the shared secret, with no lifetimes, so it is always
current. Static mode only: a session driven by bfdd takes its keys over
the data-plane socket instead. Intended for testing an authenticated
session end to end, which bfdd cannot ask this data plane to do.
.TP
.BI --log-level " error|info|debug"
Logging verbosity.
.TP
.B --check
Open the XDP object, run the ABI check, load it through the verifier,
report whether it loads and is ABI-matched on the running kernel, and
exit. Used by the package postinst and the support matrix.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdp-bfd/engine.conf
Environment file read by the systemd unit; sets XDP_BFD_ARGS.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/xdp-bfd/bfd_xdp.o
The XDP object, found by the binary with no argument.
.TP
.I /run/xdp-bfd/stats.json
Default stats output path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdp-bfd-observe (8),
.BR bfdd (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Full deployment and limitations notes are in
.IR /usr/share/doc/xdp-bfd/README.md .
The threat model and flood measurements, the RFC coverage matrix and the
list of supported kernels are kept with the project rather than shipped,
on the docs branch at
.UR https://github.com/w453y/xdp-bfd/tree/docs
.UE .
